Cleaning Robot Components & Cost Breakdown
Robot Base & Mobility

Robot chassis/platform: $30-150 (depending on size/quality)
DC motors (2-4): $5-15 each
Wheels: $10-30
Motor controllers: $15-30
Battery pack (LiPo recommended): $20-50

Object Detection & Manipulation

Camera/vision sensor: $15-60 (Raspberry Pi Camera or equivalent)
Distance sensors (ultrasonic/infrared): $3-8 each (need 3-5)
Robotic arm with gripper: $40-150 (or DIY with servos)
Servo motors (for arm joints): $5-15 each (need 3-6)

Vacuum System

Small vacuum motor: $15-40
Dust collection container: $5-15 (or repurposed container)
Filter system: $5-15

Control System & Electronics

Microcontroller (Arduino): $20-30
Single-board computer (Raspberry Pi 4): $45-80
Motor drivers: $10-20
Power distribution board: $10-25
Wires, connectors, breadboard: $15-30

Software & Programming

Programming software: Free (Arduino IDE, Python)
Computer vision libraries: Free (OpenCV)
Robot control software: Free (ROS or custom)

Additional Materials

Frame materials (aluminum, plastic, 3D printed parts): $20-50
Fasteners, screws, nuts: $10-20
3D printing filament (if using 3D printed parts): $20-30
Miscellaneous components: $20-50

Total Estimated Cost

Budget version: $250-400
Mid-range version: $400-600
Advanced version: $600-900+


Note: Costs can be reduced by salvaging parts from old electronics, using second-hand components, or simplifying certain aspects of the design.
